WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.840
Seven D Part B extends patient assessment into point-of-care diagnostics, respiratory specimens, ECGs, blood gases and focused ultrasound. This first session builds a reliable diagnostic process; the next develops the ECG and blood-gas interpretation in detail.
7D Part B把患者评估扩展到床旁检测、呼吸标本、ECG、血气及聚焦超声。本节先建立可靠诊断流程，下一节详细发展ECG和血气判读。

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:31.920
The central school sequence is recognition, interpretation and action. Finding an abnormality is the beginning: explain what it might mean, how trustworthy it is and what the patient needs next.
学校核心顺序是识别、解释、行动。发现异常只是开始：还要解释可能意义、可信程度及患者下一步需要。

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:46.008
Useful action can be immediate support, a different monitoring plan, consultation, destination coordination or a clearer handover. Ordering more tests is not automatically the most useful response.
有用行动可以是即时支持、调整监测、咨询、协调目的地或更清楚的交接，增加检查不自动是最有用反应。

00:00:46.008 --> 00:01:01.272
The saved source skips a printed section Five and does not include every promised blood-draw, urine or biomarker lesson. This course explains the recovered teaching without inventing those missing bodies or claiming a device checkoff.
保存来源的印刷编号跳过第5节，也没有每个承诺的采血、尿液或生物标志物课程正文。本课解释取得的教学，不编造缺失正文或声称设备考核已过。

00:01:01.272 --> 00:01:15.576
Start with the patient: a frightened alert person breathing deeply is different from a tired person with shallow breaths and falling awareness. The same isolated number can carry different urgency in those two encounters.
先看患者：清醒惊恐且呼吸深，与疲惫浅呼吸、意识下降的人不同。同一个孤立数值在这两种情况中的紧急程度可能不同。

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:27.840
Identify the immediate threat before selecting the device. An airway problem, ineffective ventilation or severe hemorrhage needs an effective response while the team gathers useful information.
选择仪器前先识别即时威胁。气道问题、无效通气或严重出血，需要在团队收集有用资料时同时处理。

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:42.264
Ask a focused question, such as whether a trace is interpretable, glucose is low or a trained ultrasound finding changes concern for a reversible cause. A vague search for any abnormality promotes distraction.
问题要聚焦，例如记录是否可解释、血糖是否低，或受训超声发现是否改变对可逆原因的怀疑。漫无目标寻找任何异常容易分心。

00:01:42.264 --> 00:01:53.064
When testing cannot be done safely or promptly, communicate the limitation and keep treating the clinical problem. Unavailable information is not a normal result.
无法安全及时检查时，要说明限制并继续处理临床问题。没有取得资料，不等于结果正常。

00:01:53.064 --> 00:02:05.784
A plausible-looking result may belong to the wrong patient, a different time or the wrong sample type. Confirm identity and when the information was actually obtained before building a treatment decision around it.
看似合理的结果可能属于错误患者、另一时间或错误标本类型。用它作治疗决定前，先确认身份及真正采集时间。

00:02:05.784 --> 00:02:19.104
Collection technique and handling affect validity. Contamination, an incorrectly chosen container, a delay or an unreadable label can make a technically completed test clinically misleading.
采集技术和处理会影响有效性。污染、容器选错、延误或标签不清，会让技术上已完成的检测在临床上误导。

00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:30.912
The instrument also needs its actual operating checks, approved consumables and the correct mode. A screen that powers on is not evidence that every quality-control requirement was met.
仪器也需要实际操作检查、获认可耗材及正确模式。屏幕亮起，不证明已经符合全部质控要求。

00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:43.128
Finally check units, expected range and fit with the examination. If the result conflicts with the patient, investigate the conflict rather than choosing whichever version is more convenient.
最后核对单位、预期范围及是否符合检查。结果与患者矛盾时，应追查矛盾，不能选更方便相信的那个。

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:58.896
The school discusses troponin, lactate, blood gases and ultrasound in a prehospital context. That does not establish that every PCP unit carries them or that every PCP is authorized to acquire and independently act on them.
学校在院前背景讨论肌钙蛋白、乳酸、血气和超声，但不证明每辆PCP车都有这些设备，也不证明每位PCP获准采集并独立依其行动。

00:02:58.896 --> 00:03:13.848
Separate learning the interpretation from invasive collection and device operation. A correct written answer does not establish consent, aseptic skill, sample quality, image acquisition or competence under supervision.
要区分学习解释与侵入采样、设备操作。书面回答正确，不证明已具备同意处理、无菌技能、标本质量、图像采集或受督导能力。

00:03:13.848 --> 00:03:27.432
Use the actual service protocol, endorsement and available resource. This session teaches you to recognize useful information and assist or escalate appropriately rather than creating an extra license category.
应依实际服务规程、认证及资源。本课教你识别有用资料并适当协助或升级，不创造新的执照权限。

00:03:27.432 --> 00:03:40.848
If an advanced clinician supplies a result, preserve who obtained it, the method and limitations. Receiving information does not transfer the operator responsibility to someone who did not perform the test.
高级人员提供结果时，要保留采集者、方法和限制。收到资料不表示操作者责任转给未实施检测的人。

00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:52.608
An ECG records electrical activity. A concerning pattern can support a time-critical coronary pathway, but a tracing does not directly show the clot or measure cardiac output.
ECG记录电活动。可疑模式可支持有时效性的冠脉路径，但记录不直接显示血栓，也不测心排量。

00:03:52.608 --> 00:04:06.360
A blood gas samples a particular circulation at a particular time. It contributes oxygenation, ventilation and acid-base information only when the sample type, units and treatment context are known.
血气取自某一循环、某一时间。只有知道标本类型、单位和治疗背景，才能正确提供氧合、通气及酸碱资料。

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:19.344
A biomarker can support a clinical suspicion without proving a complete diagnosis. A focused ultrasound scan answers a narrower question than a comprehensive radiology or cardiology examination.
生物标志物可支持临床怀疑，却不证明完整诊断。聚焦超声回答的问题，也比完整放射或心脏检查更窄。

00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:33.936
Combine complementary evidence rather than expecting one machine to settle every uncertainty. An organized ECG, normal saturation and some cardiac motion still require a patient-linked perfusion assessment.
应组合互补证据，不期待一台机器解决所有不确定。即使ECG有组织、饱和度正常、心脏可见活动，仍需联系患者评估灌注。

00:04:33.936 --> 00:04:46.776
Glucose testing illustrates the diagnostic process already learned in Week One. The reading is useful because the result can change an immediate decision, not because the meter is a substitute for the primary survey.
第1周血糖检测体现同样诊断流程。它有用，是因为结果能改变即时决定，而不是因为血糖仪可替代主要评估。

00:04:46.776 --> 00:04:58.560
Use an appropriate site, clean preparation, the right strip and the device instructions. Consider technique or perfusion problems when a surprising result does not fit the encounter.
应依合适部位、清洁准备、正确试纸及设备说明。意外结果与现场不符时，要考虑技术或灌注问题。

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:11.880
A patient whose glucose has improved but remains confused needs continued assessment for another or an additional cause. Correction of one abnormality is not proof that the whole illness has resolved.
血糖改善却仍混乱的患者，需要继续寻找另一病因或并存问题。纠正一个异常，不证明整个疾病已经解决。

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:22.320
Carry this discipline into unfamiliar devices: verify the result, identify the decision it supports and reassess the patient after the actual intervention.
把这种纪律用于陌生设备：核实结果，确定它支持哪个决定，并在真实干预后复评患者。

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:35.352
Troponin is a cardiac injury biomarker, not an enzyme that measures coronary flow. An elevated result needs interpretation with symptoms, ECG, timing and the actual assay pathway.
肌钙蛋白是心肌损伤标志物，不是测冠脉血流的酶。升高结果需结合症状、ECG、时间及实际检测路径解释。

00:05:35.352 --> 00:05:47.616
An early negative result cannot universally exclude infarction, and injury can occur in more than one disease. Do not equate any positive result with a definite acute coronary clot.
早期阴性不能普遍排除梗死，损伤也可见于多种疾病。不能把任何阳性都等同于确定的急性冠脉血栓。

00:05:47.616 --> 00:05:58.920
A patient with a useful diagnostic ECG and a time-critical STEMI concern should not wait for an unavailable field troponin before the indicated notification and care pathway.
ECG有用且存在紧急STEMI怀疑时，不能为等现场无法取得的肌钙蛋白而延误所需通知及照护路径。

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:12.528
The module introduces the concept, but the separate promised biomarker lesson and school analyzer details are not recovered. No assay-specific cutoff, serial schedule or discharge rule is invented here.
模块介绍这一概念，但独立的生物标志物课程及学校分析仪细节未取得。这里不会编造特定试剂阈值、连续检测时程或出院规则。

00:06:12.528 --> 00:06:26.688
The school links lactate with inadequate tissue perfusion and shock. That link is useful, but lactate can also rise through other production or clearance mechanisms; it is not exclusively a product proving anaerobic shock.
学校把乳酸联系到组织灌注不足和休克，这有帮助，但乳酸也可因其他产生或清除机制升高，不能专门当作证明无氧性休克的产物。

00:06:26.688 --> 00:06:41.688
An elevated value should prompt a serious review of circulation, breathing, history and possible causes. It cannot by itself distinguish infection, bleeding, pump failure or another stressful illness.
数值升高应促使认真检查循环、呼吸、病史及可能病因，但单独不能区分感染、失血、泵衰或其他应激疾病。

00:06:41.688 --> 00:06:57.336
The twenty twenty-six sepsis guidance also cautions against diagnosing or excluding sepsis with a single biomarker and against continuing fluids solely until lactate normalizes. Apply patient context, not a reflex number-driven treatment.
2026年脓毒症指导同样强调不能凭单一标志物确诊或排除脓毒症，也不能只为乳酸恢复正常而持续补液。应依患者背景，而不是数值触发反射治疗。

00:06:57.336 --> 00:07:10.224
When a trend is available through an authorized system, preserve sampling method, time and intervening treatment. A trend without those details can falsely appear to show improvement or deterioration.
通过获授权系统取得趋势时，要保留取样方法、时间及中间治疗，否则趋势可能假装显示好转或恶化。

00:07:10.224 --> 00:07:21.480
Before starting a test, say what decision it may change. If the result will not alter immediate care, monitoring or communication, consider whether it is the priority now.
检查前说清它可能改变什么决定。如果结果不会改变即时照护、监测或沟通，就要考虑现在是否优先。

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:32.880
Confirm that the team has the actual equipment, supplies, training and permission. A lesson title containing a diagnostic procedure does not make an unavailable service appear.
确认团队有真实设备、耗材、训练和权限。课名包含某项诊断操作，并不会使没有的服务凭空出现。

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:46.776
Allocate tasks so the diagnostic operator does not become the only person observing a deteriorating patient. Partner communication should include any falling alertness, worsening ventilation or perfusion change.
分工时不能让诊断操作者同时成为唯一观察恶化患者的人。同伴应通报意识下降、通气恶化或灌注变化。

00:07:46.776 --> 00:08:00.144
Stop or change the plan if the patient deteriorates, collection becomes unsafe or repeated attempts delay meaningful care. Record the limitation honestly rather than reporting a completed normal test.
患者恶化、采集不安全或反复尝试延误有效照护时，应停止或改计划。诚实记录限制，不能报告成检查完成且正常。

00:08:00.144 --> 00:08:14.712
The module mixes several swab depths and site names. Separate anterior nasal, mid-turbinate and nasopharyngeal sampling before discussing technique; each test must use its accepted specimen and swab.
模块混用了几种深度及部位名称。讨论技术前先分清前鼻腔、中鼻甲和鼻咽采样，每种检测都要使用其接受的标本及拭子。

00:08:14.712 --> 00:08:24.888
A short anterior nasal swab is not automatically adequate for an NP order, and pushing an unsuitable swab deeper does not convert it into a safe NP kit.
短的前鼻腔拭子不自动足以完成鼻咽医嘱，把不合适拭子推得更深，也不能变成安全鼻咽试剂盒。

00:08:24.888 --> 00:08:37.728
Throat and combined throat-nasal collection are different validated methods, not a universal instruction to use one swab in both places. Check the test and receiving laboratory instructions.
咽部及咽鼻联合采样属于不同验证方法，不是通用的一根拭子两处擦指令。要核对检测及接收实验室说明。

00:08:37.728 --> 00:08:49.272
Do not memorize the source one-to-two, five-to-six and two-to-five centimeter statements as one procedure. Patient anatomy and the actual approved kit determine the method.
不能把来源中的1至2、5至6及2至5厘米混成一套操作。患者解剖及真实获认可试剂盒决定方法。

00:08:49.272 --> 00:09:00.720
Explain why the specimen is being requested and what the person may feel. Use clear language and allow questions instead of presenting a swab as a surprise during another assessment.
解释为何需要标本及可能感觉。语言要清楚，并允许提问，不能在另一项评估中突然拿拭子上去。

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:12.096
Confirm consent and cooperation through the appropriate process. Tell the patient how to signal that they need you to stop; a frightened patient may move suddenly if that plan is missing.
应依适当流程确认同意和配合。告诉患者怎样示意需要停止，否则恐惧时可能突然移动。

00:09:12.096 --> 00:09:26.520
Recent facial trauma, severe nosebleeding or abnormal nasopharyngeal anatomy require caution and the actual clinician or laboratory pathway. Do not force a routine NP approach through a problem you have not assessed.
近期面部创伤、严重鼻出血或鼻咽解剖异常，需要谨慎并依真实临床或实验室路径。不能对尚未评估的问题强行套常规鼻咽方法。

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:39.840
Choose safe positioning and support appropriate to age, ability and clinical state. A sample is not worth compromising the airway, causing a preventable injury or delaying an emergency intervention.
体位和支持应适合年龄、能力及临床状态。不能为一份标本损害气道、造成可避免伤害或延误急救。

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:52.584
Assess infection risk and use the current service precautions before collection. The school mention of an apron or a mask only if indicated is not a complete universal respiratory-sampling protection plan.
采集前应评感染风险并使用现行服务防护。学校提到围裙或按需口罩，不是一套完整通用的呼吸标本防护计划。

00:09:52.584 --> 00:10:09.888
BCCDC distinguishes ordinary NP or throat collection precautions from aerosol-generating procedures. Gown, gloves, mask and eye protection appear in its swab guidance; task, pathogen and local policy can require different protection.
BCCDC区分常规鼻咽或咽采样与产气溶胶操作。其拭子指导包括隔离衣、手套、口罩及眼防护，具体任务、病原体及当地政策可能要求不同保护。

00:10:09.888 --> 00:10:21.720
Arrange a clean preparation area and avoid touching sterile tips or contaminating the collection tube. Keep used supplies away from shared monitor controls, paperwork and clean equipment.
应安排清洁准备区，避免碰无菌头或污染采样管。用过耗材要与共用监护按键、文件及清洁器材分开。

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:35.040
After collection, secure the specimen and remove PPE through the correct process. Hand hygiene remains necessary after glove removal, and contaminated equipment needs the approved cleaning method.
采集后应固定标本并依正确程序脱防护。脱手套后仍需手卫生，污染器材要用获认可清洁方法。

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:49.392
Check the requested test, patient and accepted collection site. A respiratory PCR sent to a laboratory is not necessarily an immediate point-of-care result simply because the specimen was obtained beside the patient.
核对所需检测、患者及获接受取样部位。在患者旁取得标本，不表示送实验室的呼吸PCR就是即时床旁结果。

00:10:49.392 --> 00:11:03.504
Prepare the specified swab, container and transport medium if required. Check expiry and package integrity; do not substitute a visually similar kit without confirmation that the test accepts it.
准备指定拭子、容器及需要时的转运液。检查有效期和包装完整性，未经确认不能用外观相似试剂盒替换。

00:11:03.504 --> 00:11:15.912
Use the required identifiers and match the requisition to the patient and tube. The collection site and time matter because two otherwise similar specimens can answer different questions.
使用所需身份标识，并使申请单、患者和试管一致。部位及时间很重要，外观相同的两份标本可能回答不同问题。

00:11:15.912 --> 00:11:27.240
Do the identification check at the bedside and follow the actual labelling workflow. Do not carry an anonymous specimen away and rely on memory to repair identity later.
应在床旁核对身份并依真实标记流程，不要先带走匿名标本，再靠记忆补身份。

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:38.592
For an NP collection performed by a trained authorized person, the path follows the nasal floor toward the posterior target, rather than pointing upward toward the bridge of the nose.
受训且获授权人员实施鼻咽采样时，路径沿鼻底朝后方目标，而不是向鼻梁上方戳。

00:11:38.592 --> 00:11:51.816
The April twenty twenty-six PHO NP-kit instructions use a flexible mini-tip swab, a parallel-to-palate path and an anatomical endpoint rather than one universal fixed depth for every patient.
2026年4月PHO鼻咽试剂盒说明使用柔性小头拭子，路径平行上腭，并依解剖终点，而不是给所有患者一个固定深度。

00:11:51.816 --> 00:12:03.480
That is a specific kit example, not confirmation that the school uses the same swab, head angle or method. Use the actual approved instructions and supervised skill teaching.
这只是具体试剂盒示例，不证明学校使用相同拭子、头角度或方法。应依实际获认可说明和受督导技能教学。

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:15.672
Never overcome unexpected resistance by pushing harder. Stop, reassess and obtain the appropriate help or alternate plan when tolerance or anatomy makes collection unsafe.
不能靠更用力克服异常阻力。耐受或解剖使采样不安全时，应停止、重评，并获得适当帮助或替代计划。

00:12:15.672 --> 00:12:27.120
Open the supplies aseptically and hold the shaft without touching the collection tip. Maintain patient support and explain the next step while protecting the prepared specimen surface.
无菌打开耗材，握杆时不碰采样头。应维持患者支持、解释下一步，同时保护准备好的采样表面。

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:38.784
Use the site-specific technique taught with that kit. Rotation, contact time and whether one or both nostrils are used are not interchangeable instructions across every swab type.
应使用与该试剂盒配套教学的部位特定技术。转动、接触时间及单侧或双侧鼻孔，并不是所有拭子都通用的指令。

00:12:38.784 --> 00:12:51.744
Observe discomfort, bleeding, movement and breathing during collection, then withdraw gently as instructed. If the patient becomes unstable, return immediately to the clinical priorities.
采集时观察不适、出血、移动及呼吸，再依说明轻柔退出。患者不稳定时，应立即回到临床优先事项。

00:12:51.744 --> 00:13:05.496
Place the specimen into the specified container and close it safely. A shaft is broken only at the designed point when that kit calls for it; never improvise a sharp broken end or an unsealed container.
将标本放入指定容器并安全关闭。只有试剂盒要求时，才在设计折点折杆；不能临时制造尖锐断端或留下未封容器。

00:13:05.496 --> 00:13:17.400
The source says specimens are usually kept at room temperature, but that is not a universal rule. The PHO NP example differentiates unused-kit storage from refrigeration of a collected specimen.
来源称标本通常放室温，但这不是通用规则。PHO鼻咽示例明确区分未用试剂盒储存，与采后标本冷藏。

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:31.224
Check the actual test and receiving laboratory requirements for temperature, maximum delay and transport medium. Do not invent a freezing instruction when the test or available transport system is different.
要核对实际检测及接收实验室的温度、最长延误和转运液要求。检测或可用转运系统不同，不能编造冷冻指令。

00:13:31.224 --> 00:13:45.576
Seal and package the specimen using the approved system, with completed paperwork protected from leakage. BCCDC requires suitable containers and regulated packaging rather than an ordinary unprotected bag.
应依获认可系统封闭并包装标本，完整文件要防漏液污染。BCCDC要求合适容器及合规包装，不是普通无保护袋子。

00:13:45.576 --> 00:13:57.000
Document collection and dispatch details, and confirm the handoff to the authorized receiver. A specimen left on a counter is not evidence of completed laboratory receipt.
记录采集及送出细节，并确认向获授权接收者交接。把标本留在台面，不证明实验室已收到。

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:07.464
A positive result may support the suspected infection, but detection does not prove that every symptom is caused by that organism or that no second illness is present.
阳性可能支持怀疑感染，但检出不证明全部症状都由该病原体造成，也不证明没有第二种疾病。

00:14:07.464 --> 00:14:19.944
A negative result depends on specimen quality, timing, site and test performance. It cannot universally exclude infection or justify ignoring a high-risk clinical presentation.
阴性依赖标本质量、时间、部位及检测性能，不能普遍排除感染，更不能让你忽视高风险临床表现。

00:14:19.944 --> 00:14:31.824
An invalid result is not a negative result. Follow the specified repeat or laboratory pathway, and do not repeatedly recollect in a way that delays urgent patient care.
无效不等于阴性。应依规定的复检或实验室路径，也不能反复重采而延误紧急患者照护。

00:14:31.824 --> 00:14:43.488
Pending means unknown. Maintain the indicated clinical and infection-control plan, then communicate the result and its limits when it becomes available through the correct channel.
待出结果就是未知。应维持有指征的临床及感染控制计划，再通过正确渠道传达取得的结果和限制。

00:14:43.488 --> 00:14:57.648
If a sterile tip touches an unsuitable surface before collection, do not continue as though nothing happened. A contaminated surface can produce a misleading specimen even if the collection feels technically smooth.
无菌头在采集前碰到不合适表面，不能当没事继续。即使采集过程很顺，污染表面仍可能造成误导标本。

00:14:57.648 --> 00:15:10.680
A leaking tube or mismatched identity is a validity and exposure problem, not a cosmetic defect to hide. Keep the team informed and use the actual replacement or laboratory process.
试管漏液或身份不匹配，是有效性及暴露问题，不是要藏起的小外观缺陷。应告知团队并依实际替换或实验室程序处理。

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:19.992
Do not solve an identity uncertainty by guessing a name or changing the time to make the paperwork fit. Preserve what is known and obtain appropriate help.
不能靠猜姓名或改时间，让文件看着匹配。应保留已知事实并取得适当帮助。

00:15:19.992 --> 00:15:29.760
Return to the patient priorities while the specimen issue is resolved. Technical perfection is not achieved by leaving a deteriorating person unattended.
处理标本问题时仍要回到患者重点。让恶化患者无人照看，并不算技术完美。

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:41.760
Point-of-care ultrasound uses focused bedside imaging to support a particular decision. It is not a replacement for the primary survey or the same as a comprehensive specialist examination.
床旁超声用聚焦床边影像支持某个具体决定，不能替代主要评估，也不等于完整专科检查。

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:53.976
The question may concern pleural movement, cardiac motion or a vessel for a trained access procedure. Choose a question that the operator and available equipment can actually answer.
问题可以涉及胸膜移动、心脏活动，或受训穿刺操作中的血管。应选择操作者及现有设备真正能回答的问题。

00:15:53.976 --> 00:16:06.888
The school label POCUS for PCPs teaches concepts, not blanket permission. Training, local scope, device approval and continuing image-quality processes still determine who performs the examination.
学校名为POCUS for PCPs是在教概念，不是全面授权。训练、当地权限、设备认可及持续图像质控，仍决定谁能实施。

00:16:06.888 --> 00:16:15.600
A scan can be limited or indeterminate. Report that honestly; failure to obtain a useful view is not a negative study.
扫描可以受限或不能确定，应诚实报告。未取得有用切面，不等于阴性检查。

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:27.984
An ultrasound image depends on probe location, orientation, settings and the tissue being sampled. A familiar shape on the wrong view can be misidentified with great confidence.
超声图像依赖探头位置、方向、设定及所取组织。在错误切面中，熟悉形状也可能被非常自信地认错。

00:16:27.984 --> 00:16:41.784
Before interpreting motion, identify the intended anatomical structure. Superficial muscle movement is not automatically pleural sliding, and any round dark structure is not automatically a safe vein.
解释移动前，先确认目标解剖。浅层肌肉活动不自动是胸膜滑动，圆形暗结构也不自动是安全静脉。

00:16:41.784 --> 00:16:54.024
B mode displays a cross-sectional brightness image; M mode displays change along a selected line over time. The line position and correct structure determine what an M-mode pattern means.
B模式显示断面亮度图，M模式显示选定一条线随时间的变化。线的位置及结构是否正确，决定M模式图案意义。

00:16:54.024 --> 00:17:06.648
This is conceptual preparation, not a substitute for supervised scanning with the actual probe and equipment. Static diagrams cannot demonstrate image acquisition or needle-tip control.
这是概念准备，不能替代使用实际探头器材的受督导扫描。静态图也不能证明图像采集或针尖控制能力。

00:17:06.648 --> 00:17:18.888
Lung sliding refers to the respiratory movement of opposed pleural surfaces. The important first step is recognizing the actual pleural interface rather than a moving superficial tissue layer.
肺滑动指相贴胸膜面随呼吸移动。首要是识别真实胸膜界面，而不是移动的浅表组织层。

00:17:18.888 --> 00:17:32.592
When correctly identified, sliding supports apposition at the sampled location. It does not certify that every other region of the lung is free of pneumothorax or that the patient has no other respiratory emergency.
正确识别的滑动支持取样位置胸膜相贴，但不能证明肺的其他全部区域没有气胸，也不能证明没有其他呼吸急症。

00:17:32.592 --> 00:17:44.400
Reduced visible movement can reflect the breathing state, location, technique or disease. A patient who is apneic may not create the expected respiratory movement.
可见移动减少可能与呼吸状态、位置、技术或疾病有关。呼吸暂停患者可能没有预期的呼吸运动。

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:55.248
Use the finding as one part of a focused assessment and describe exactly where and how it was obtained. Do not replace the examination with the phrase sliding present.
应把这一发现作为聚焦评估的一部分，并准确说明位置和获取方式。不能用一句滑动存在替代患者检查。

00:17:55.248 --> 00:18:05.376
In the school comparison, the seashore pattern reflects movement below the pleural line on M mode, while the stationary tissues above remain more linear.
学校比较中，M模式海岸征反映胸膜线以下移动形成纹理，上方较静止组织则更像水平线。

00:18:05.376 --> 00:18:17.184
Barcode and stratosphere are two names for a more uniformly linear pattern when the sampled pleural movement is absent. The pattern alone does not specify why movement is absent.
条码征与平流层征是同一类更均一线状图案的两个名称，见于所取胸膜移动缺失；图案单独不能指定为何不移动。

00:18:17.184 --> 00:18:28.584
A wrong M-mode cursor, inadequate view or very limited respiratory motion can mislead. First validate the acquisition, then consider the possible physiology.
M模式取线错误、切面不足或呼吸运动很少，都可误导。应先核实采集，再考虑可能生理。

00:18:28.584 --> 00:18:40.104
Do not turn the school visual association into barcode equals pneumothorax. State the observed sign separately from the suspected diagnosis and the action the whole patient requires.
不能把学校图示关联简化成条码等于气胸。应把观察征象、怀疑诊断及整位患者需要的行动分别说清。

00:18:40.104 --> 00:18:53.712
Pneumothorax is air in the pleural space. A true lung point is a transition between regions with and without pleural apposition and can provide highly specific supporting evidence in the appropriate examination.
气胸是胸膜腔内有空气。真正肺点是胸膜相贴与不相贴区域间的交界，在适当检查中可提供特异性很高的支持证据。

00:18:53.712 --> 00:19:06.960
Absent sliding has other causes, including apnea, prior pleural adhesion or a ventilated lung not receiving airflow. Absence of a visible lung point does not safely exclude pneumothorax.
滑动缺失还有其他原因，包括呼吸暂停、既往胸膜粘连或受通气患者某侧肺未得到气流。没看到肺点也不能安全排除气胸。

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:21.312
Tension physiology means pressure is impairing breathing and circulation, including venous return. A stable-looking ultrasound label is not a substitute for recognizing a patient becoming profoundly hypoperfused.
张力生理表示压力正在损害呼吸和循环，包括静脉回流。一个看着稳定的超声标签，不能替代识别严重低灌注中的患者。

00:19:21.312 --> 00:19:33.840
Follow the actual trained emergency pathway and intervention authority. A deteriorating patient should not wait for an unavailable or repeated scan when the clinical indication already requires urgent care.
应依真实受训急救路径及干预权限。临床指征已要求紧急照护时，不能让恶化患者等不存在或反复的扫描。

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:46.080
The school glossary calls white-out lung a nonspecific appearance where normal motion is difficult to see. That conflates brightness and motion and should not be used as a diagnostic definition.
学校词汇表把白肺写成不容易看到正常移动的非特异外观，这混淆了亮度和运动，不能用作诊断定义。

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:59.808
Describe the actual visual pattern instead. Extensive or coalescent vertical artifacts may create a bright interstitial pattern, but distribution, pleural features and the clinical state remain important.
应描述真实图案。广泛或融合的垂直伪影可形成明亮间质图案，但分布、胸膜特点及临床状态仍重要。

00:19:59.808 --> 00:20:10.536
Such patterns are not unique to cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Other interstitial, inflammatory or traumatic disease can create overlapping appearances.
这种图案并非心源性肺水肿独有，其他间质、炎症或创伤疾病也可有重叠外观。

00:20:10.536 --> 00:20:20.616
Report a limited or uncertain interpretation rather than treating a white screen as permission for a particular drug, positive-pressure strategy or destination.
解释受限或不确定时要如实报告，不能把屏幕白当成某种药、正压策略或目的地的许可。

00:20:20.616 --> 00:20:33.672
The school introduces vein compressibility as a clue for ultrasound-guided access. A normally patent vein often collapses with gentle pressure, whereas an artery is generally less compressible.
学校把静脉可压缩性作为超声引导穿刺线索。通常通畅静脉在轻压下可塌陷，动脉一般较不易压缩。

00:20:33.672 --> 00:20:44.736
This is not an absolute identification rule. A thrombosed vein may not compress, and a low-pressure artery or excessive probe pressure can undermine the simple comparison.
这不是绝对身份规则。血栓静脉可能不塌，低压动脉或探头用力过大，也会破坏简单比较。

00:20:44.736 --> 00:20:54.768
Combine anatomy, course, wall appearance, pulsatility and the methods included in actual training. Compressibility does not prove that the full needle path is safe.
应结合解剖、走行、管壁、搏动及实际训练中的方法。能压扁不证明整条进针路径安全。

00:20:54.768 --> 00:21:07.416
A focused access scan is not automatically a formal DVT exclusion study. A normal-looking short segment cannot clear an entire limb or a patient with suspected pulmonary embolism.
聚焦穿刺扫描不自动等于正式排除DVT检查。短段看似正常，不能排除整条肢体或疑肺栓塞患者的问题。

00:21:07.416 --> 00:21:23.352
Ultrasound-guided IV access can help identify an appropriate vessel when performed within an authorized, supervised competency pathway. The technology does not remove the ordinary need for indication, consent and asepsis.
在获授权、受督导能力路径内，超声引导IV可帮助识别合适血管，但不会取消指征、同意和无菌要求。

00:21:23.352 --> 00:21:32.928
The operator must understand the chosen view and locate the advancing needle tip, not merely see a bright portion of shaft and assume the tip is safe.
操作者必须理解所选切面并定位前进针尖，不能只看到一段亮针杆就假设针尖安全。

00:21:32.928 --> 00:21:45.000
A stored vessel image is not real-time guidance. Uncontrolled advancement can still injure an artery, nerve or deeper structure, even when the selected vessel looked suitable earlier.
保存的血管图片不是实时引导。即使先前目标血管合适，失控前进仍可伤动脉、神经或深部结构。

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:58.488
After placement, verify through the actual access protocol, secure and reassess. This lesson explains the risk and reasoning; it does not certify ultrasound cannulation from a screen.
置管后应依实际通路规程确认、固定并复评。本课解释风险与推理，不能凭屏幕授予超声穿刺能力。

00:21:58.488 --> 00:22:13.056
A patient can have organized electrical activity without effective circulation. Visible cardiac movement adds information about mechanical activity but does not by itself prove adequate forward flow or a palpable pulse.
患者可有组织电活动却没有有效循环。可见心脏移动增加机械活动资料，但本身不证明向前血流足够或一定摸得到脉搏。

00:22:13.056 --> 00:22:24.360
Pseudo PEA describes a pulseless presentation with visible cardiac activity. The term does not authorize abandoning the clinical arrest pathway because the heart appears to move.
Pseudo PEA描述无脉表现却可见心脏活动。这个词不授权你只因心脏看着在动就放弃临床骤停路径。

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:38.328
Apparent cardiac standstill also depends on the quality and timing of the view. It must not be the sole reason for termination, and isolated right ventricular dilation does not prove pulmonary embolism during arrest.
看似心脏静止也依赖切面质量和时间。它不能作为唯一停止复苏理由；骤停中单独右室扩大，也不能证明肺栓塞。

00:22:38.328 --> 00:22:52.248
Use the local resuscitation and consultation process, including its role-specific permissions. Understanding an ultrasound term does not replace the required termination or recognition-of-life-extinct criteria.
应依当地复苏及咨询流程，包括角色特定权限。理解超声术语，不能替代所需的终止复苏或生命消逝确认条件。

00:22:52.248 --> 00:23:04.128
High-quality compressions and indicated defibrillation remain priorities. A diagnostic task that adds prolonged no-flow time can undermine the resuscitation it was intended to help.
高质量按压及有指征除颤仍是优先。诊断任务若增加长时间无血流，会损害本来想帮助的复苏。

00:23:04.128 --> 00:23:15.600
Only a trained authorized operator should integrate an intra-arrest scan. The team must plan the question and coordinate it with the actual resuscitation process before any interruption.
只有受训获授权操作者才能整合骤停超声。任何中断前，团队必须先计划问题并与实际复苏流程协调。

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:26.664
Do not prolong a rhythm or pulse assessment while searching for a better image. Resume compressions on time and accept that an attempted scan may remain inconclusive.
不能为找更好图像而延长心律或脉搏评估。要及时恢复按压，并接受此次扫描可能仍无定论。

00:23:26.664 --> 00:23:40.440
The twenty twenty-five resuscitation ultrasound guidance explicitly rejects additional or prolonged compression interruptions. It is a safety cross-check here, not permission to import a different country drug or termination algorithm.
2025年复苏超声指导明确反对额外或延长按压中断。这里用作安全核对，不是允许导入另一国家的用药或终止算法。

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:53.808
Week Six asks for a primary problem, a complicating problem and a deliberate what else check. Diagnostic information should strengthen that process, not encourage fixation on the first abnormality.
第6周要求找主要问题、复杂因素，并主动问还有什么。诊断资料应加强这一流程，而不是让你固着于首个异常。

00:23:53.808 --> 00:24:07.032
A patient can have a respiratory infection and a coronary event, or chronic heart disease and acute traumatic bleeding. A positive swab or known ECG history does not make the other threats disappear.
患者可同时有呼吸感染和冠脉事件，也可有慢性心脏病及急性创伤出血。拭子阳性或已知ECG史，不会让其他威胁消失。

00:24:07.032 --> 00:24:18.264
Say which finding changes an immediate action and which remains a hypothesis. Uncertainty should be clear enough that the partner and receiving team can help resolve it.
要说清哪个发现改变即时行动，哪个仍是假设。不确定性要表达得足够清楚，让同伴及接收团队能协助解决。

00:24:18.264 --> 00:24:29.928
Repeated primary assessment is the anchor when the data become complex. A clever interpretation is not successful if it misses a patient losing ventilation or perfusion.
资料复杂时，反复主要评估是锚点。解释再聪明，若漏掉患者正失去通气或灌注，也不算成功。

00:24:29.928 --> 00:25:25.368
Connect the recovered diuretic paragraph to the actual medicine history. Loop drugs reduce salt reabsorption in the ascending loop and can increase potassium loss; thiazides act farther downstream in the distal tubule and also commonly waste potassium. Potassium-sparing drugs reduce distal potassium loss through different targets, including aldosterone blockade or a direct distal-tubular effect; they do not all simply increase potassium reabsorption. Renal impairment and additional potassium-raising medicines can make retention dangerous. Selected potassium-wasting and potassium-sparing drugs may be intentionally combined, but this does not make combining two potassium-sparing agents safe. Spironolactone and triamterene are not interchangeable products. Assess the actual plan and patient rather than assuming potassium and volume will balance.
把找回的利尿药段连到真实药史：袢利尿药减少升支盐重吸收，并可增加排钾；噻嗪作用于更下游远曲小管，也常丢钾。保钾药经不同靶点减少远端钾丢失，包括醛固酮阻断或直接远端肾小管作用，并非都简单增加钾重吸收。肾损害及其他升钾药可使保留变危险；选定丢钾药与保钾药可能有意合用，但这不表示两种保钾药合用安全。螺内酯与氨苯蝶啶也不是可互换产品，应评真实计划及患者，不能假设钾和容量必然平衡。

00:25:25.368 --> 00:26:12.480
Apply that mechanism to an original transfer: a breathless patient has a prescribed infusion, poor recent intake and several diuretics. Do not decide from ankle edema alone that more diuresis is needed, or from thirst alone that a large bolus is safe. Establish actual recent doses, losses, prescribed restrictions, renal history and available laboratory context; trace the infusion, check the site and rate, and reassess breathing, mentation and perfusion. Explain the competing fluid and electrolyte risks in the handover. An unfamiliar drug name or a single serum result is a reason to verify, not permission to stop, replace or add a medicine independently.
用于原创转运病例：气促患者有既有输注、近期摄入差，并用数种利尿药。不能只看踝肿就认定还需利尿，也不能只凭口渴就认定大量推液安全。应确认近期真实剂量、丢失、规定限制、肾史及可得化验背景；追踪输注，查部位及速度，并复评呼吸、意识及灌注。交接应解释相互竞争的液体和电解质风险。不熟悉药名或单个血液结果提示核查，不授权独立停、换或加药。

00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:26.424
Start with the patient state and immediate threat, then report the useful diagnostic evidence. Include sample or view type, time and any important quality limitation rather than a bare number or disease label.
先报患者状态和即时威胁，再报有用诊断证据。应包括标本或切面类型、时间及重要质量限制，而不是裸数或疾病名称。

00:26:26.424 --> 00:26:37.512
Separate what you observed from what you suspect. For example, an absent-sliding finding in one limited view is not the same sentence as confirmed tension pneumothorax.
要分开观察到什么与怀疑什么。例如一个受限切面中滑动缺失，与已证实张力性气胸不是同一句话。

00:26:37.512 --> 00:26:51.624
Describe actual interventions and patient responses, including treatments not given for a known reason. Do not let a test handover conceal the airway, perfusion or transport actions that matter more urgently.
说明实际干预及患者反应，包括因已知原因未给的治疗。不能让检查交接遮住更紧急的气道、灌注或转运动作。

00:26:51.624 --> 00:27:03.672
Finish with the required request and confirm receipt. Preserve the record and trace or result through the approved information system; sending is not proof of receiving or transfer of care.
最后提出所需请求并确认收到。应通过获认可信息系统保留记录、波形或结果，发送不等于接收，也不等于照护责任已转。

00:27:03.672 --> 00:27:17.280
In an original rehearsal, a sixty-seven-year-old at a community music rehearsal has fever, cough and breathlessness. The person is now cool, fatigued and describes pressure rather than a sharp chest pain.
原创演练中，一位67岁患者在社区音乐排练时发热、咳嗽且气促，现在皮肤冷、疲惫，描述胸部压迫感而非锐痛。

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:27.528
A previously collected respiratory specimen has a positive result. That supports one part of the history but does not explain away new perfusion or chest symptoms.
此前采集呼吸标本的结果阳性，支持部分病史，但不能解释掉新的灌注或胸部症状。

00:27:27.528 --> 00:27:42.456
Assess primary threats and obtain useful observations and an interpretable ECG while arranging the indicated care and conveyance. Do not announce uncomplicated infection merely because a test has a name.
应评估主要威胁，取得有用观察和可解释ECG，同时安排所需照护及转运。不能只因检测有个病原名称，就宣布单纯感染。

00:27:42.456 --> 00:27:53.688
The case is original practice, not a school assessment answer. Explain the primary concern, the infection as a possible contributor and what else remains dangerous.
这是原创练习，不是学校考核答案。应解释主要担忧、感染可能如何参与，以及还有哪些危险问题。

00:27:53.688 --> 00:28:06.720
Now change only the clinical state: the same patient becomes less responsive and breaths become shallow. A pending repeat diagnostic test must not distract the team from this deterioration.
现在只改变临床状态：同一患者反应下降、呼吸变浅。等待中的复检不能让团队忽视这种恶化。

00:28:06.720 --> 00:28:19.080
Reassess airway, ventilation and circulation immediately and provide the effective trained support required. A normal earlier oxygen saturation does not prove the new breathing is adequate.
应立即重评气道、通气及循环，并提供所需的有效受训支持。早先饱和度正常，不能证明现在呼吸足够。

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:31.560
Announce the change clearly, allocate tasks and seek the appropriate additional resource. The operator can pause a lower-priority diagnostic task so the patient does not lose a rescuer.
要清楚宣布变化、分工并请求适当额外资源。操作者可暂停较低优先诊断任务，不能让患者少一个救援者。

00:28:31.560 --> 00:28:42.336
Recheck measurement quality and preserve the actual sequence in the record. The important learning is adapting the plan when the patient changes, not defending the first interpretation.
应重查测量质量并在记录中保留真实顺序。重点是随患者变化改计划，不是维护第一次解释。

00:28:42.336 --> 00:28:54.120
For a swab rehearsal, identify the requested site and show the correct kit and labelling plan before approaching a simulated patient. Explain when you would stop rather than forcing collection.
拭子演练应先确定所需部位、展示正确试剂盒及标签计划，再接近模拟患者，并解释何时停止而非强采。

00:28:54.120 --> 00:29:07.176
For a POCUS discussion, state the question, view and operator limits. A conceptual answer should distinguish a visible sign from the disease and from an authorized intervention.
POCUS讨论要说出问题、切面及操作者限制。概念回答需区分可见征象、疾病和获授权干预。

00:29:07.176 --> 00:29:20.832
Ask a partner to introduce one problem: an identity mismatch, an unusable view or a deteriorating patient. Explain how the workflow changes without hiding uncertainty or abandoning immediate care.
让同伴引入一个问题：身份不符、切面不可用或患者恶化。应解释流程如何改变，不藏不确定，也不放弃即时照护。

00:29:20.832 --> 00:29:34.320
The actual school kit, analyzer, ultrasound equipment and competence rubric remain separate requirements. Reading and rehearsal prepare you to learn that skill; they do not replace its supervised assessment.
真实学校试剂盒、分析仪、超声设备及能力评分表，仍是独立要求。阅读和演练帮助学习技能，不能替代受督导评估。

00:29:34.320 --> 00:29:44.496
You should now be able to explain why a reliable result needs the right patient, method, quality and time. A completed button sequence is not enough.
现在应能解释，可靠结果为何需要正确患者、方法、质量及时间。完成一串按键还不够。

00:29:44.496 --> 00:29:58.464
Separate swab sites, follow the actual kit and laboratory process, and distinguish positive, negative, invalid and pending results. Protect the patient and the specimen identity throughout.
应区分拭子部位、遵循实际试剂盒及实验室流程，并分清阳性、阴性、无效及待结果，始终保护患者及标本身份。

00:29:58.464 --> 00:30:11.160
Explain lung sliding, M-mode patterns, vessel clues and cardiac motion with their limitations. No isolated sign grants a diagnosis, invasive procedure or termination decision.
应能解释肺滑动、M模式图案、血管线索及心脏活动，同时说出局限。孤立征象不授予诊断、侵入操作或停止复苏决定。

00:30:11.160 --> 00:30:25.104
Use the bilingual glossary to check the terminology, then move to the blood-gas and ECG session. Keep recognition, interpretation and action connected to a patient rather than to a collection of isolated facts.
可用中英词汇导读核对术语，再进入血气及ECG课程。要让识别、解释和行动始终联系患者，而不是堆积孤立知识点。
